# Week 2 Task: Statistical Analysis and Visualization (Healthcare)

Statistical analysis of a **simulated** hospital dataset (200 patients, no real patient data).

## Files
| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `Statistical_Analysis_Report.docx` | Main deliverable: analytical report 
| `generate_data_week2.py` | Creates the synthetic dataset |
| `data/patients_week2.csv` | Simulated data |
| `analysis.py` | Runs statistics and builds charts |
| `charts/` | Five PNG visualizations |
| `results.json` | Test statistics produced by the script |

## Methods
Descriptive statistics, Shapiro-Wilk, Pearson/Spearman correlation, Welch's t-test, Mann-Whitney U, chi-square, one-way ANOVA, linear regression.

## Run
```
pip install pandas numpy scipy matplotlib
python generate_data_week2.py
python analysis.py
```
